  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you’ve picked out your new bathroom countertop – awesome! Now you’re probably wondering what the actual installation process looks like. We try to make it as smooth as possible, and generally, here’s how it goes. First, we'll do a site visit to get super accurate measurements and create a template. This is where we discuss everything from the edge profile and backsplash height to your sink type and faucet hole layout. Getting these details right upfront prevents any surprises later on. Once the template is done, your countertop goes into fabrication, which means cutting it to size, adding cutouts for your sink and faucet, and finishing the edges. For the install day, we'll need you to clear a path and protect any adjacent surfaces. We'll also ask you to remove items from your cabinets and disconnect the plumbing beforehand. We usually handle the removal of your old top. Then, we’ll level the vanity, dry-fit the new top to ensure a perfect fit, and secure it with silicone adhesive. For undermount sinks, we'll attach those with clips and silicone, and caulk any seams or the backsplash. Finally, you’ll need a plumber to reconnect your fixtures. We’ll also walk you through care instructions and any warranty info. The whole process, from template to final install, can take a few weeks for custom stone, so patience is key! If you're ready to get started, give us a call."
    }
  ],
